1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,487
On Thursday, Outlook simply stopped working for people around the world.

2
00:00:04,537 --> 00:00:11,649
About 130,000 users had reported Outlook problems on Downdetector, CNBC said.

3
00:00:11,699 --> 00:00:13,445
And it wasn't just email.

4
00:00:13,495 --> 00:00:18,409
Teams, SharePoint, Copilot and Defender were on Microsoft's list too.

5
00:00:18,459 --> 00:00:23,981
Microsoft says some servers unexpectedly went offline, and the rest got overloaded.

6
00:00:24,031 --> 00:00:27,153
It is now reverting a recent network change.

7
00:00:27,203 --> 00:00:30,506
Microsoft says there's no sign of a cyber attack.

8
00:00:30,556 --> 00:00:36,622
But the root cause isn't confirmed, and at the time of writing there's no time for a full fix.

9
00:00:36,672 --> 00:00:38,119
Oh, hi Muja.

10
00:00:38,169 --> 00:00:39,803
So what should you do?

11
00:00:39,853 --> 00:00:44,522
Don't reinstall Outlook, because the problem is on Microsoft's side.

12
00:00:44,572 --> 00:00:48,206
Teams chat and SharePoint files mostly kept working.

13
00:00:48,256 --> 00:00:50,109
My take: keep a plan B.

14
00:00:50,159 --> 00:00:55,563
A phone tree, a second chat app, and a contact list that lives outside the suite.

15
00:00:55,613 --> 00:00:58,554
Microsoft says recovery will be gradual.

16
00:00:58,604 --> 00:01:01,470
Updates and the full story are on my blog.
